# Rust build artifacts
target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# darkmux runtime state (project-local + defense-in-depth)
.darkmux/
# Root-scoped only (not `runs/`, unqualified) — an unqualified pattern here
# matched ANY directory literally named `runs` anywhere in the tree, which
# silently swallowed `ui/src/lenses/runs/` (the Packet 3 runs-lens source)
# from `git status`/`git add` with zero error output. Found live: `git
# status` showed every other new file in this packet except that directory.
/runs/
sandboxes/
*.trajectory.jsonl
qa-reply.json
qa-reply.err
cpu-samples.txt

# Run-artifact dirs — keep them out of committed fixtures (a committed one
# trips `lab doctor`'s cleanliness check + the workspace test). Mirrors the
# canonical RUN_ARTIFACT_DIRS the lab clone prunes + the hash excludes.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
coverage/
.coverage
.darkmux-runtime/
.darkmux-agent/

# dotenv files (local secrets)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

# Viewer e2e (Playwright) — local artifacts
tests/e2e/node_modules/
tests/e2e/.served/
tests/e2e/test-results/
tests/e2e/playwright-report/
target-review/

# Viewer parity harness (Packet 0a) — local artifacts. corpus/ and goldens/
# ARE committed (they're the recorded spec the React port is graded
# against); only the build/run scratch below is ignored.
tests/parity/node_modules/
# GLOBBED, not enumerated. The list used to name each suite's served dir, so a
# new one — `.served-next-probe/`, staged by a review agent instrumenting this
# tree — was not ignored and got swept into a commit by a `git add -A`,
# carrying a 152-line copy of the whole viewer bundle. A pattern that has to be
# extended by hand every time a suite is added will eventually not be.
tests/parity/.served-next*/
tests/parity/.gallery/
tests/parity/corpus.tmp-*/
tests/parity/test-results/
tests/parity/playwright-report/

# Flatsat (Packet 0b) — local artifacts. .state/ is the seeded/bind-mounted
# DARKMUX_HOME for each container (regenerated every `up` by seed.mjs from
# the parity corpus + a hand-authored peer fixture); never committed.
tests/flatsat/node_modules/
tests/flatsat/.state/
tests/flatsat/test-results/
tests/flatsat/playwright-report/
tests/flatsat/.gallery/

# UI port scaffold (Packet 1) — local artifacts. `ui/dist/index.html` is
# copied to the COMMITTED `crates/darkmux-serve/assets/next.html` by
# `bun run build`'s `copy-artifact` step; `dist/` itself is scratch.
# `src/types/generated/` IS committed (ts-rs output; see ui/README.md).
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/
ui/test-results/
ui/playwright-report/
ui/verify/test-results/
ui/verify/playwright-report/
ui/verify/.gallery/

# Playwright scratch at the REPO ROOT. The rules above cover
# `tests/parity/`, `tests/e2e/`, `tests/flatsat/` and `ui/`, but not the root —
# so `test-results/.last-run.json` (a stale failed-run marker) sat tracked from
# 2026-08-04. Root-scoped deliberately; see the `/runs/` note above for what an
# unqualified pattern does in this tree.
/test-results/

# Agent + session scratch. `.scratch/` held a commit message, a PR body, two
# `gh issue view` dumps and a one-off smoke driver — all committed 2026-08-08
# and referenced by nothing. Scratch belongs in the session scratchpad, not in
# a public repo's history.
.scratch/
*.scratch
*.scratch.*

# cargo-mutants run output — local build logs (accidentally committed in #1636)
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Demo-env output (scripts/demo-env/) — generated fixtures + the shot PNGs.
# Root-scoped, per the `/runs/` note above. The INPUTS are committed
# (world.json, sessions/, the scripts); everything derived from them is not,
# so a re-shoot never shows up as a diff.
/screenshots/
